WEBVTT

00:07.746 --> 00:09.183
- Are you ready, kids?
- 孩子们，你们准备好了吗？

00:09.270 --> 00:10.706
All:
Aye, aye, Captain!
全部：
是啊是啊，队长！

00:10.793 --> 00:12.360
- I can't hear you.
- 我听不到你说话。

00:12.447 --> 00:14.231
All:
Aye, aye, Captain!
全部：
是啊是啊，队长！

00:14.318 --> 00:17.495
- ♪ Ohh... ♪
- ♪ 哦...♪

00:17.582 --> 00:19.236
♪ Who lives in a pineapple
under the sea? ♪
♪ 谁住在菠萝里
在海底？ ♪

00:19.323 --> 00:21.630
All:
SpongeBob SquarePants!
全部：
海绵宝宝！

00:21.717 --> 00:23.414
- ♪ Absorbent and yellow
and porous is he ♪
- ♪ 吸水性和黄色
他是多孔的 ♪

00:23.501 --> 00:25.329
all:
SpongeBob SquarePants!
全部：
海绵宝宝！

00:25.416 --> 00:27.288
- ♪ If nautical nonsense
be something you wish ♪
- ♪ 如果航海废话
成为你想要的东西♪

00:27.375 --> 00:29.681
all:
SpongeBob SquarePants!
全部：
海绵宝宝！

00:29.768 --> 00:31.553
- ♪ Then drop on the deck
and flop like a fish ♪
- ♪ 然后落在甲板上
然后像鱼一样扑通扑通♪

00:31.640 --> 00:33.250
all: SpongeBob SquarePants!
- Ready?
所有：海绵宝宝！
- 准备好？

00:33.337 --> 00:34.991
All:
SpongeBob SquarePants!
全部：
海绵宝宝！

00:35.078 --> 00:37.428
SpongeBob SquarePants!
海绵宝宝！

00:37.515 --> 00:39.343
SpongeBob SquarePants!
海绵宝宝！

00:39.430 --> 00:40.736
- SpongeBob
- 海绵宝宝

00:40.823 --> 00:42.564
SquarePants!
方裤！

00:42.651 --> 00:45.175
[laughing]
[笑]

00:45.262 --> 00:47.569
[flute playing]
[长笛演奏]

00:47.656 --> 00:48.874
[waves crashing]
[海浪拍打]

00:50.702 --> 00:53.575
[jaunty music]
[欢快的音乐]

00:53.662 --> 00:59.972
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

01:00.060 --> 01:04.238
- ♪ Oh happy birthday on you ♪
- ♪ 哦，祝你生日快乐 ♪

01:04.325 --> 01:07.284
♪ It's your birthday,
it's true ♪
♪ 这是你的生日，
这是真的♪

01:07.371 --> 01:11.158
♪ It's the day
that I built you ♪
♪ 这一天
我创造了你♪

01:11.245 --> 01:13.812
♪ Happy birthday on ♪
♪ 生日快乐 ♪

01:13.899 --> 01:17.729
[screaming]
[尖叫]

01:19.166 --> 01:20.602
[groans]
[呻吟]

01:20.689 --> 01:22.256
- Oh, Sheldon.
- 哦，谢尔顿。

01:22.343 --> 01:25.911
This has been the best
birthday I've ever had.
这已经是最好的了
我曾经过的生日。

01:27.913 --> 01:29.915
- And it ain't over yet.
- 事情还没有结束。

01:30.002 --> 01:33.745
It's time for the birthday
girl to open her presents.
又到了生日的时间了
女孩打开她的礼物。

01:33.832 --> 01:35.399
[grunting]
[咕噜声]

01:35.486 --> 01:37.184
Ta-da.
哒哒。

01:37.271 --> 01:40.274
- Oh?
- 哦？

01:40.361 --> 01:46.236
- It's a gift certificate
for tango lessons.
- 这是一张礼券
探戈课。

01:46.323 --> 01:49.196
- Oh, you know I'd love
to dance with you, sweetie,
- 哦，你知道我会喜欢
和你一起跳舞，亲爱的，

01:49.283 --> 01:51.676
but we've tried this before.
但我们之前已经尝试过。

01:51.763 --> 01:53.243
And if you recall...
如果你还记得...

01:53.330 --> 01:54.244
- Yeah?
- 是的？

01:54.331 --> 01:55.550
Oh, yeah?
哦，是吗？

01:55.637 --> 01:57.334
Yee-haw.
呀呀。

01:57.421 --> 01:59.467
[whistle tooting]
[吹口哨]

01:59.554 --> 02:02.034
- It did not go well.
- 进展并不顺利。

02:02.122 --> 02:05.473
- This time is going
to be different.
- 这一次即将过去
变得不同。

02:05.560 --> 02:10.565
Because your other
birthday present is this.
因为你的另一个
生日礼物是这个。

02:10.652 --> 02:13.133
The Leg Yanker Five Zillion.
腿扬克五亿。

02:13.220 --> 02:17.093
[grunting]
[咕噜声]

02:17.180 --> 02:18.790
This is for you, baby.
这是给你的，宝贝。

02:18.877 --> 02:20.618
[grunting]
[咕噜声]

02:20.705 --> 02:23.621
[dramatic music]
[戏剧音乐]

02:23.708 --> 02:25.232
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

02:25.319 --> 02:28.800
[grunting]
[咕噜声]

02:28.887 --> 02:31.847
[screams]
[尖叫声]

02:31.934 --> 02:34.328
[sighs]
[叹气]

02:36.765 --> 02:37.853
- Oh.
- 哦。

02:37.940 --> 02:40.464
- Hmm, nice weather up here.
- 嗯，这里天气很好。

02:40.551 --> 02:42.074
Whoa.
哇哦。

02:42.162 --> 02:45.948
- Well, hello, tall,
green, and evil.
- 嗯，你好，高个子，
绿色，邪恶。

02:46.035 --> 02:49.778
- May I have this dance?
- 我可以跳一支舞吗？

02:49.865 --> 02:53.042
- [grunting]
- [咕哝]

02:58.134 --> 03:00.267
- Love the new stems, Plankton.
- 喜欢新茎，浮游生物。

03:00.354 --> 03:01.398
Whoa.
哇哦。

03:01.485 --> 03:03.008
- It's 8:00 p.m. already.
- 现在是晚上 8:00已经。

03:03.095 --> 03:04.401
Where's our dance instructor?
我们的舞蹈老师在哪里？

03:04.488 --> 03:06.577
- Hello, class.
- 你好，同学们。

03:06.664 --> 03:09.580
[upbeat music]
[欢快的音乐]

03:09.667 --> 03:16.283
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

03:20.504 --> 03:24.334
[cheers and applause]
[欢呼和掌声]

03:25.205 --> 03:26.423
- [sighs]
- [叹气]

03:26.510 --> 03:29.513
- I'm your tango
instructor, Susie Groove.
- 我是你的探戈
教练，苏西·格鲁夫。

03:29.600 --> 03:33.822
And when I'm done with you,
this is how you gotta move.
当我和你结束后
这就是你必须采取的行动方式。

03:33.909 --> 03:37.086
[grunting]
[咕噜声]

03:41.090 --> 03:44.833
So everyone start dancing,
and I'll come
于是大家开始跳舞，
我会来

03:44.920 --> 03:46.748
around and give you some tips.
周围并给你一些提示。

03:46.835 --> 03:49.577
- ♪ Ahh ahh ahh,
la la la la la la la la ♪
- ♪ 啊啊啊啊，
啦啦啦啦啦啦啦♪

03:49.664 --> 03:52.057
- You're breaking
the first rule, honey.
- 你打破了
第一条规则，亲爱的。

03:52.144 --> 03:53.972
It takes two to tango.
探戈需要两个人。

03:54.059 --> 03:55.887
- Sorry, Miss Groove.
- 对不起，格鲁夫小姐。

03:55.974 --> 03:57.802
Mr. Krabs ordered me to be
Pearl's tango partner tonight,
蟹老板命令我
今晚珍珠的探戈舞伴，

03:57.889 --> 04:01.110
but she just doesn't
dig my tangy moves.
但她就是不
挖掘我的刺激动作。

04:01.197 --> 04:03.286
- SpongeBob, you can't tango.
- 海绵宝宝，你不会探戈。

04:03.373 --> 04:05.114
I need a real dance partner,
我需要一个真正的舞伴

04:05.201 --> 04:07.986
not a cackling,
bow-legged goofball.
不是咯咯笑声，
弓腿傻瓜。

04:08.073 --> 04:09.205
No offense.
无意冒犯。

04:09.292 --> 04:10.859
- I took it as a compliment.
- 我把它当作一种恭维。

04:10.946 --> 04:12.295
[cackles]
[咯咯笑]

04:12.382 --> 04:15.167
- I can teach anyone to tango.
- 我可以教任何人探戈。

04:15.255 --> 04:17.474
All you gotta do is...
你所要做的就是...

04:17.561 --> 04:20.477
[upbeat music]
[欢快的音乐]

04:20.564 --> 04:23.872
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

04:23.959 --> 04:27.310
- Wow, you can tango.
- 哇，你会探戈。

04:27.397 --> 04:29.747
Thanks to Susie Groove.
感谢苏西·格鲁夫。

04:29.834 --> 04:33.229
- [grunting]
- [咕哝]

04:33.316 --> 04:36.406
- That's too close to tango.
- 这太接近探戈了。

04:36.493 --> 04:43.457
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

04:43.544 --> 04:44.849
- One, two, three.
- 一二三。

04:44.936 --> 04:46.024
One, two, three.
一二三。

04:46.111 --> 04:47.678
Relax, Sheldon.
放松点，谢尔顿。

04:47.765 --> 04:50.638
- I'm trying,
my little whirling dervish,
- 我正在努力，
我的旋转小苦行僧，

04:50.725 --> 04:54.555
but these legs
have minds of their own.
但这些腿
有自己的主见。

04:54.642 --> 04:56.208
Not that way, you idiots.
不是这样的，你们这些白痴。

04:56.296 --> 04:57.209
Damn you.
该死的你。

04:57.297 --> 04:58.820
Hya!
哈！

04:58.907 --> 05:00.865
- Compose yourself, darling.
- 冷静点，亲爱的。

05:00.952 --> 05:03.607
We're in public.
我们在公共场合。

05:03.694 --> 05:05.087
- I know.
- 我知道。

05:05.174 --> 05:07.132
I just need something
to balance me.
我只是需要一些东西
来平衡我。

05:07.219 --> 05:07.872
See?
看？

05:07.959 --> 05:09.439
It works.
有用。

05:09.526 --> 05:10.484
Uh-oh.
呃哦。

05:10.571 --> 05:14.662
Wait, I got it.
等等，我明白了。

05:14.749 --> 05:16.272
I got it.
我得到了它。

05:16.359 --> 05:19.884
[screams]
[尖叫声]

05:19.971 --> 05:23.279
- Stop dancing!
- 别跳舞了！

05:23.366 --> 05:25.760
- Ow.
- Sorry, Susie.
- 噢。
- 对不起，苏西。

05:25.847 --> 05:28.458
- I just washed my legs, and
I can't do a thing with them.
- 我刚刚洗了腿，然后
我对他们无能为力。

05:28.545 --> 05:30.460
- Legs ain't your
problem, honey.
- 腿不是你的
问题，亲爱的。

05:30.547 --> 05:32.984
If you want to tango,
you got to learn
如果你想跳探戈，
你必须学习

05:33.071 --> 05:35.857
to dance with your hips.
用你的臀部跳舞。

05:35.944 --> 05:37.337
- With my lips?
- 用我的嘴唇？

05:40.731 --> 05:41.993
This isn't working.
这不起作用。

05:42.080 --> 05:43.299
- Ugh.
- 呃。

05:43.386 --> 05:45.475
- That's because I said hips.
- 那是因为我说的是臀部。

05:45.562 --> 05:46.302
Watch me.
看着我。

05:46.389 --> 05:48.130
All you got to do is...
你所要做的就是...

05:48.217 --> 05:51.089
[percussive music]
[打击乐]

05:51.176 --> 05:54.310
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

05:54.397 --> 05:56.704
- Wow, your hips are so hip.
- 哇，你的臀部太时髦了。

05:56.791 --> 05:59.837
You got your work
cut out for you, Sheldon.
你得到了你的工作
谢尔顿，适合你。

05:59.924 --> 06:01.186
- My hips can't do that.
- 我的臀部做不到这一点。

06:01.273 --> 06:02.579
- Of course they can.
- 他们当然可以。

06:02.666 --> 06:04.538
You got to force them to do it.
你必须强迫他们这样做。

06:04.625 --> 06:08.629
The tango is physical,
emotional,
探戈是身体性的，
情绪化,

06:08.716 --> 06:12.546
and most importantly,
aggressive.
最重要的是，
具有侵略性。

06:12.633 --> 06:13.851
- What?
- 什么？

06:13.938 --> 06:15.505
Aggressive?
挑衅的？

06:15.592 --> 06:18.421
Now you're talking my language.
现在你正在说我的语言。

06:18.508 --> 06:21.729
- Yeah,
we speak fluent aggression.
- 是的，
我们说着流利的攻击性语言。

06:21.816 --> 06:23.252
- Good.
- 好的。

06:23.339 --> 06:26.037
Tap into that aggression
and put it in your hips.
利用这种攻击性
并把它放在你的臀部。

06:26.124 --> 06:27.822
Now, abrazo.
现在，阿布拉索。

06:27.909 --> 06:29.737
Embrace.
拥抱。

06:29.824 --> 06:30.868
Both: Abrazo.
两人：阿布拉索。

06:30.955 --> 06:31.956
- Ready?
- 准备好？

06:32.043 --> 06:33.436
All you gotta do is...
你所要做的就是...

06:33.523 --> 06:35.873
- Terrific tangoing, Planktons.
- 很棒的探戈，浮游生物。

06:35.960 --> 06:36.918
- Yeah.
- 是的。

06:37.005 --> 06:38.354
I thought we were good.
我以为我们很好。

06:38.441 --> 06:42.402
- Oh, how nice of you to say.
- 哦，你说得真好。

06:42.489 --> 06:44.708
[yells]
[喊叫]

06:44.795 --> 06:48.059
- Abrazo, my stinky cheese.
- 阿布拉索，我的臭奶酪。

06:48.146 --> 06:51.889
- Abrazo, my rotten rose.
- 阿布拉索，我的烂玫瑰。

06:51.976 --> 06:56.590
- Oh, no, I accidentally
dropped my spike strip.
-哦，不，我不小心
我的钉条掉了。

06:56.677 --> 06:58.505
Oopsie.
哎呀。

06:58.592 --> 07:03.466
- [yells]
- [大喊]

07:05.076 --> 07:06.904
[piano trill]
[钢琴颤音]

07:06.991 --> 07:10.125
[piano music]
[钢琴音乐]

07:10.212 --> 07:13.041
[both chuckling]
[两人都笑了]

07:13.128 --> 07:16.392
- We're the king
and queen of tango.
- 我们是国王
和探戈女王。

07:16.479 --> 07:17.959
- OK, Planktons, take four.
- 好吧，浮游生物，拿四个。

07:18.046 --> 07:19.351
Ahh!
啊！

07:22.790 --> 07:25.488
- That wasn't very nice
of Plankton and Karen.
- 那不太好
浮游生物和凯伦。

07:25.575 --> 07:28.926
- No, it wasn't,
but that's the tango, honey.
- 不，不是的，
但这就是探戈，亲爱的。

07:29.013 --> 07:31.320
- [laughs]
- [笑]

07:31.407 --> 07:32.626
- Bravo, Planktons.
- 太棒了，浮游生物。

07:32.713 --> 07:34.802
Nice aggression.
很好的侵略性。

07:34.889 --> 07:36.543
- Oh, thank you, Susie.
-哦，谢谢你，苏西。

07:36.630 --> 07:40.024
I haven't had this much fun
since I got defragged.
我还没玩过这么多乐趣
自从我整理碎片后。

07:40.111 --> 07:43.463
- I'd say we're the best
in the class, wouldn't you,
- 我想说我们是最好的
在课堂上，你不是吗

07:43.550 --> 07:44.986
Miss Groove?
格鲁夫小姐？

07:45.073 --> 07:47.771
- I think you're both great,
but my top students
- 我认为你们都很棒
但我的尖子生

07:47.858 --> 07:49.251
might disagree.
可能不同意。

07:49.338 --> 07:51.166
Both: Top students?
两人：尖子生？

07:51.253 --> 07:52.254
- Yeah.
- 是的。

07:52.341 --> 07:55.387
They're late today.
他们今天迟到了。

07:55.475 --> 07:58.260
- The tango masters
have arrived.
- 探戈大师
已经到了。

07:58.347 --> 07:59.783
- Sorry we're late.
- 抱歉我们迟到了。

07:59.870 --> 08:02.569
Bubble Bass needed
clean underwear.
需要泡泡鲈鱼
干净的内衣。

08:02.656 --> 08:03.439
- Mother.
- 母亲。

08:03.526 --> 08:05.876
- Bubble Bass and his mom?
- 泡泡巴斯和他的妈妈？

08:05.963 --> 08:07.748
- That's right.
- 这是正确的。

08:07.835 --> 08:10.446
Mother and I have won the
Undersea Tango Championship
我和妈妈赢得了
海底探戈锦标赛

08:10.533 --> 08:12.796
three years in a row.
连续三年。

08:12.883 --> 08:14.755
We're the best.
我们是最好的。

08:14.842 --> 08:19.324
- But yet somehow, and without
warning, we're the best!
- 但不知何故，而且没有
警告，我们是最棒的！

08:19.411 --> 08:21.849
- I smell a dance-off.
- 我闻到了跳舞的味道。

08:21.936 --> 08:24.808
- Insects first.
- 首先是昆虫。

08:24.895 --> 08:26.854
Hmph.
哼。

08:26.941 --> 08:32.686
[both grunting]
[两人都咕哝着]

08:32.773 --> 08:34.557
Ta-da.
哒哒。

08:34.644 --> 08:38.169
Well, try and out-tango that.
好吧，尝试跳探戈吧。

08:38.256 --> 08:40.650
- Don't mind if we do.
- 如果我们这样做的话，不要介意。

08:40.737 --> 08:47.614
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

08:51.966 --> 08:52.923
- Huh?
- 啊？

08:53.010 --> 08:55.447
[both growling]
[双方咆哮]

08:55.535 --> 08:57.537
- I said we're the best.
- 我说过我们是最好的。

08:57.624 --> 08:58.886
Abrazo.
阿布拉索。

08:58.973 --> 09:02.106
- Looks like someone
ordered a Bass sandwich.
- 看起来像某人
点了一份巴斯三明治。

09:02.193 --> 09:04.805
[both yelling]
[两人大喊]

09:04.892 --> 09:06.676
- Well, that was fun.
- 嗯，那很有趣。

09:06.763 --> 09:08.722
But I guess we're
not aggressive enough
但我想我们是
不够激进

09:08.809 --> 09:09.897
to be the best.
成为最好的。

09:09.984 --> 09:12.943
- Nobody is more
aggressive than us.
- 没有人比他更
比我们侵略性。

09:13.030 --> 09:14.684
They just have more practice.
他们只是有更多的练习。

09:14.771 --> 09:18.340
If only there was some way
we could cheat and show them
如果有什么办法就好了
我们可以欺骗并向他们展示

09:18.427 --> 09:20.255
who's really the best.
谁才是真正最好的。

09:20.342 --> 09:22.344
- Let's just go home, Sheldon.
- 我们回家吧，谢尔顿。

09:22.431 --> 09:24.999
Here,
this fell out of your pocket.
在这里，
这是从你口袋里掉出来的。

09:25.086 --> 09:28.393
- Ooh, it's my Ray-Ray ray,
the device
- 哦，这是我的射线，射线，
该设备

09:28.480 --> 09:32.572
that turns me into my alter
ego with great hair, Ray-Ray.
这让我变成了我的分身
拥有漂亮头发的自我，雷雷。

09:32.659 --> 09:34.965
That'll make me more aggressive.
这会让我变得更有攻击性。

09:35.052 --> 09:37.141
- Ooh, you're right, Plankton.
- 哦，你说得对，浮游生物。

09:37.228 --> 09:40.667
My Ray-Ray is the only one
who could take charge of this.
我的雷雷是唯一的
谁能负责这件事。

09:40.754 --> 09:41.668
Hold still.
保持不动。

09:45.019 --> 09:47.195
- It's Ray-Ray, baby.
- 这是雷雷，宝贝。

09:47.282 --> 09:48.239
- Oops.
- 哎呀。

09:48.326 --> 09:51.242
Sorry, wrong old man.
对不起，老哥，看错了。

09:53.549 --> 09:57.292
- It's Ray-Ray, baby.
- 这是雷雷，宝贝。

09:57.379 --> 09:59.207
- [grunting]
- [咕哝]

09:59.294 --> 10:03.515
- Looks like someone ordered
a cold plate of revenge.
- 看起来有人订购了
复仇的冷盘。

10:03.603 --> 10:06.431
- With extra humiliation.
- 带着额外的羞辱。

10:06.518 --> 10:07.955
[both hissing]
[两人都发出嘶嘶声]

10:08.042 --> 10:10.087
- Tango rematch, honey.
- 探戈复赛，亲爱的。

10:10.174 --> 10:13.874
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

10:13.961 --> 10:16.877
- [grunting]
- [咕哝]

10:23.057 --> 10:24.928
[laughter]
[笑声]

10:25.015 --> 10:28.105
- No.
- 不。

10:28.192 --> 10:30.238
- Whoo!
- 呼！

10:30.325 --> 10:32.283
- Whoa!
[laughs]
- 哇！
[笑]

10:32.370 --> 10:33.328
Whoo!
呼！

10:33.415 --> 10:35.591
Go, Ray-Ray, go.
走吧，雷雷，走吧。

10:38.159 --> 10:43.381
- I want to hate the
Planktons, but they're so good.
- 我想讨厌
浮游生物，但它们太棒了。

10:43.468 --> 10:45.601
- Oh, there, there, there.
- 哦，那里，那里，那里。

10:45.688 --> 10:48.212
- He dances like an angel.
- 他跳舞得像个天使。

10:48.299 --> 10:50.432
- Of death.
- 死亡。

10:50.519 --> 10:55.437
- By the tango vested in me,
I pronounce Karen and Ray-Ray
- 以我赋予的探戈，
我发音为Karen 和Ray-Ray

10:55.524 --> 10:58.440
my top students, honey.
我的尖子生，亲爱的。

10:58.527 --> 11:00.007
- We did it, Ray-Ray.
- 我们做到了，雷雷。

11:00.094 --> 11:01.661
We're the best.
我们是最好的。

11:01.748 --> 11:05.360
- Happy birthday,
Karen-cakes, top of the world.
- 生日快乐，
凯伦蛋糕，世界之巅。

11:05.447 --> 11:08.842
Now for the big finish.
现在是大结局。

11:08.929 --> 11:10.408
Oh, no.
哦，不。

11:10.495 --> 11:15.022
Too much friction.
摩擦力太大。

11:15.109 --> 11:16.066
Oh my...
哦天哪...

11:16.153 --> 11:17.633
- My legs!
- 我的腿！

11:17.720 --> 11:20.854
Sorry, that's my line.
抱歉，这是我的台词。

11:20.941 --> 11:22.986
- Here, Plankton,
you can borrow my legs.
- 在这里，浮游生物，
你可以借用我的腿。

11:23.073 --> 11:24.379
- No, thanks.
- 不，谢谢。

11:24.466 --> 11:26.250
Mine are growing back already.
我的已经长回来了。

11:27.948 --> 11:29.471
Thank you, Karen.
谢谢你，凯伦。

11:29.558 --> 11:31.952
- It takes two to tango.
- 探戈需要两个人。

11:32.039 --> 11:35.825
Come here, Ray-Ray.
过来，雷雷。

11:40.308 --> 11:43.137
All: The name's Ray-Ray, baby.
全体：宝贝，我的名字叫雷雷。

11:43.224 --> 11:44.442
Both: Uh-oh.
两人：呃哦。

11:47.663 --> 11:50.535
[light bouncy music]
[轻快活泼的音乐]

11:50.622 --> 11:57.455
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

11:59.327 --> 12:00.632
- Huh?
- [panting]
- 啊？
- [气喘吁吁]

12:00.720 --> 12:02.896
Hmm?
唔？

12:02.983 --> 12:05.420
- Mmm.
- 嗯。

12:05.507 --> 12:06.813
- [munching]
- [咀嚼]

12:06.900 --> 12:08.205
Mm-hmm.
嗯嗯。

12:08.292 --> 12:11.252
I just love breakfast.
我就是喜欢早餐。

12:17.301 --> 12:20.783
- I don't mind overpaying
if it's breakfast.
- 我不介意多付钱
如果是早餐的话。

12:20.870 --> 12:23.394
- Ooh, that money looks tasty.
- 哦，那钱看起来很好吃。

12:23.481 --> 12:24.918
- Do you mind?
- 你介意吗？

12:25.005 --> 12:26.571
- Sorry.
- 对不起。

12:26.658 --> 12:28.922
All these people eating
breakfast is making me hungry.
这些人都在吃饭
早餐让我饿了。

12:29.009 --> 12:33.056
Hungry for more customers
that is.
渴望更多客户
也就是说。

12:33.143 --> 12:36.886
- Speaking of customers,
stop bothering mine.
- 说到客户，
别再打扰我的了。

12:36.973 --> 12:40.585
- Ahh!
- 啊！

12:40.672 --> 12:42.413
- Well,
that sure kick-started my day.
- 嗯，
这确实开启了我的一天。

12:42.500 --> 12:43.806
- Morning, Mr. Krabs.
- 早上好，蟹老板。

12:43.893 --> 12:45.895
- Good morning, Krusty crew.
- 早上好，Krusty 船员。

12:45.982 --> 12:48.855
I have a fantastic
idea for me restaurant.
我有一个很棒的
我的想法餐厅。

12:48.942 --> 12:51.248
- We're opening
a Krusty Krab on the moon?
- 我们要开业了
月球上的蟹堡王？

12:51.335 --> 12:53.294
- We're closing down forever?
- 我们要永远关门了？

12:53.381 --> 12:55.252
[loud explosion]
[爆炸声]

12:55.339 --> 12:57.211
- What? No.
- 什么？不。

12:57.298 --> 13:00.780
From now on, the Krusty Krab
will start serving breakfast.
从现在开始，蟹堡王
将开始供应早餐。

13:00.867 --> 13:03.739
And you two get to come
to work even earlier.
你们两个一定要来
甚至更早去上班。

13:03.826 --> 13:05.306
- Hmm?
- 唔？

13:05.393 --> 13:09.092
- Oh, boy, I get to make
Krabby Patties for breakfast.
- 哦，孩子，我要做
早餐吃蟹肉饼。

13:09.179 --> 13:10.615
- No, no, no, no, no.
- 不，不，不，不，不。

13:10.702 --> 13:12.269
People don't want
patties in the morning.
人们不想要
早上吃肉饼。

13:12.356 --> 13:14.881
They want bacon
and eggs and hash browns.
他们想要培根
还有鸡蛋和薯饼。

13:14.968 --> 13:16.578
You know, breakfast stuff.
你知道，早餐的东西。

13:16.665 --> 13:19.407
See if you can whip up
a stack of pancakes, boy-o.
看看你能不能振作起来
一堆煎饼，男孩。

13:19.494 --> 13:20.408
- Yes, sir.
- 是的，先生。

13:20.495 --> 13:25.108
[panting]
[气喘吁吁]

13:25.195 --> 13:27.197
[bell dings]
[铃声]

13:27.284 --> 13:30.287
- Give it the old mouth test,
Mr. Squidward.
- 进行旧口测试，
章鱼哥先生。

13:36.424 --> 13:39.644
- These pancakes taste
like a Krabby Patty.
- 这些煎饼的味道
就像蟹肉饼一样。

13:42.169 --> 13:43.605
- Oh.
- 哦。

13:43.692 --> 13:45.825
I guess I only know how
to cook Krabby Patties.
我想我只知道如何
煮蟹黄饼。

13:45.912 --> 13:47.914
- Oh, I was afraid of this.
- 哦，我很害怕这个。

13:48.001 --> 13:49.567
Go down to the bookstore
and pick up the breakfast
下楼去书店
并拿起早餐

13:49.654 --> 13:51.134
cookbook I ordered.
我订购的食谱。

13:51.221 --> 13:54.921
You need to expand your
repertoire a bit, boy-o.
你需要扩展你的
有点曲目，男孩。

13:57.706 --> 14:00.665
- Hello, I'm here to pick
up a cookbook for Mr. Krabs.
- 你好，我是来挑选的
为蟹老板准备一本食谱。

14:00.752 --> 14:02.363
- Well, of course, sir.
- 嗯，当然，先生。

14:02.450 --> 14:04.321
[chuckles]
[笑声]

14:04.408 --> 14:10.980
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

14:17.552 --> 14:20.294
Here you go.
干得好。

14:20.381 --> 14:23.253
- Are you sure
this is the right book?
- 你确定吗
这是正确的书吗？

14:23.340 --> 14:26.430
- Looks right to me.
- 对我来说看起来不错。

14:30.826 --> 14:33.263
- Whoops, pardon me.
- 哎呀，请原谅我。

14:33.350 --> 14:35.526
- What a polite
little hunk of cheese.
- 多么有礼貌啊
小块奶酪。

14:35.613 --> 14:37.659
[cackles]
[咯咯笑]

14:37.746 --> 14:41.489
I have a book on hold, last
name Witch, first name Evil.
我有一本书搁置，最后
名字女巫，名字邪恶。

14:41.576 --> 14:42.838
- Certainly.
- 当然。

14:47.277 --> 14:49.453
Must be this one.
一定是这个。

14:49.540 --> 14:51.716
Your book, ma'am.
你的书，女士。

14:51.803 --> 14:53.980
- I forgot my spectacles.
- 我忘记戴眼镜了。

14:54.067 --> 14:56.591
Hey, buddy, you sure this
is the magic book I ordered?
嘿，伙计，你确定这个
是我订购的魔法书吗？

14:58.636 --> 15:00.856
- Pretty sure.
- 很确定。

15:00.943 --> 15:01.639
- Huh?
- 啊？

15:01.726 --> 15:04.468
If you say so.
如果你这么说的话。

15:08.124 --> 15:10.648
- Uh-oh.
- 呃哦。

15:10.735 --> 15:13.173
[all grumbling]
[大家都在抱怨]

15:16.828 --> 15:18.830
- I got the cookbook,
Mr. Krabs.
- 我拿到了食谱，
蟹老板。

15:18.918 --> 15:20.310
- Hurry up, boy-o.
- 快点，男孩。

15:20.397 --> 15:23.444
Breakfast don't last
all day, you know.
早餐不持久
一整天，你知道。

15:26.664 --> 15:33.106
- Love potions, summoning
demons, the undead and you.
- 爱情魔药，召唤
恶魔、亡灵和你。

15:33.193 --> 15:34.629
Oh, breakfast.
哦，早餐。

15:34.716 --> 15:36.718
"Stacks of woe."
“成堆的祸患。”

15:36.805 --> 15:38.676
That must mean pancakes.
那一定是指煎饼。

15:38.763 --> 15:41.897
This book sure calls
for some weird ingredients.
这本书确实呼吁
一些奇怪的成分。

15:41.984 --> 15:44.552
Mr. Krabs, do we have
any zombie teeth,
蟹老板，我们有吗？
任何僵尸牙齿，

15:44.639 --> 15:47.424
dragon's breath, eye of newt?
龙息，蝾螈之眼？

15:47.511 --> 15:49.426
- Well, there should be some
in the back of the freezer.
- 嗯，应该有一些
在冰箱的后面。

15:49.513 --> 15:50.427
- Really?
- 真的吗？

15:50.514 --> 15:51.820
- What?
- 什么？

15:51.907 --> 15:53.517
I can't pass up a sale.
我不能错过促销。

15:53.604 --> 15:55.084
- Found them.
- 找到他们了。

15:57.434 --> 16:00.176
Must be cooked
in an iron cauldron.
一定要煮熟
在铁锅里。

16:00.263 --> 16:02.309
Ooh, classy.
哦，优雅。

16:02.396 --> 16:04.746
I think there's one
in here somewhere.
我认为有一个
在这里的某个地方。

16:04.833 --> 16:06.487
Oh, there you are.
哦，你来了。

16:06.574 --> 16:07.836
[grunts]
[咕哝]

16:12.623 --> 16:15.844
[humming]
[嗡嗡声]

16:26.420 --> 16:28.770
[muffled scream]
[低沉的尖叫声]

16:32.426 --> 16:34.994
- Oh, they're glorious.
- 哦，他们很光荣。

16:36.996 --> 16:37.648
- Hmm.
- 唔。

16:37.735 --> 16:39.085
Looks tasty.
看起来很好吃。

16:39.172 --> 16:43.915
Mr. Squidward, you're up again.
章鱼哥先生，你又起来了。

16:44.003 --> 16:46.788
- Say, these are pretty good.
- 说吧，这些都很好。

16:46.875 --> 16:48.746
Breakfast is served.
供应早餐。

16:48.833 --> 16:51.967
[cheers and applause]
[欢呼和掌声]

16:56.406 --> 16:59.279
- Your oatmeal, sir.
- 你的燕麦片，先生。

16:59.366 --> 17:00.584
- Mmm.
- 嗯。

17:00.671 --> 17:03.674
Deliciously bland.
味道清淡可口。

17:05.763 --> 17:09.202
- I woke up
before noon for this?
- 我醒了
中午之前就为了这个？

17:09.289 --> 17:12.379
Where is my morning sustenance?
我早上的食物在哪里？

17:12.466 --> 17:16.513
- Your waffles.
- 你的华夫饼。

17:16.600 --> 17:19.777
- A meal most toothsome.
- 一顿最美味的饭菜。

17:19.864 --> 17:21.866
Time to pay for my repast.
是时候付我的饭钱了。

17:23.607 --> 17:25.305
Ow.
噢。

17:25.392 --> 17:29.178
Egad, my hindquarters
have gone rogue.
埃加德，我的后躯
已经变得无赖了。

17:31.963 --> 17:34.227
- I am beyond offended.
- 我非常生气。

17:38.100 --> 17:42.626
- [howls]
- [嚎叫]

17:42.713 --> 17:46.326
- [hisses]
- [嘶嘶声]

17:46.413 --> 17:47.327
- Whoa.
- 哇哦。

17:47.414 --> 17:48.719
Whoa.
哇哦。

17:48.806 --> 17:50.156
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa, whoa.
哇，哇，哇，
哇，哇，哇。

17:50.243 --> 17:52.680
- Who ordered the parfait?
- 谁点了冻糕？

17:52.767 --> 17:58.120
[all shouting, howling]
[大家大喊大叫，嚎叫]

17:58.207 --> 18:02.124
- Huh? Huh? Huh?
- 啊？啊？啊？

18:02.211 --> 18:03.299
Of course.
当然。

18:03.386 --> 18:07.782
- Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
- 哇，哇，哇，哇。

18:07.869 --> 18:09.349
- SpongeBob.
- 海绵宝宝。

18:09.436 --> 18:11.481
What the ham and eggs
is going on around here?
火腿和鸡蛋是什么
这附近有什么事吗？

18:11.568 --> 18:14.223
- Oh, I don't think I've got
the hang of this breakfast
- 哦，我想我没有
这顿早餐的窍门

18:14.310 --> 18:16.791
thing, Mr. Krabs.
事情，蟹老板。

18:16.878 --> 18:19.489
- [chattering]
- [喋喋不休]

18:19.576 --> 18:21.100
- A cup of milk?
- 一杯牛奶？

18:21.187 --> 18:22.275
Two eggs?
两个鸡蛋？

18:22.362 --> 18:23.928
A loaf of bread?
一条面包？

18:24.015 --> 18:27.671
And kelp sugar?
还有海带糖？

18:27.758 --> 18:30.370
Eh, all right.
呃，好吧。

18:30.457 --> 18:31.414
Shoo.
嘘。

18:31.501 --> 18:34.678
French toast?
法式吐司？

18:34.765 --> 18:36.202
Hash browns?
薯饼？

18:36.289 --> 18:37.507
Quiche?
乳蛋饼？

18:37.594 --> 18:39.770
Huevos rancheros?
休沃斯牧场主？

18:39.857 --> 18:41.511
What the heck?
到底是什么？

18:41.598 --> 18:45.211
What's wrong with this
blasted spell book?
这是怎么回事
该死的咒语书？

18:45.298 --> 18:47.604
"Uncle Jimmy's Breakfast Magic"?
《吉米叔叔的早餐魔法》？

18:47.691 --> 18:49.563
It's a cookbook.
这是一本食谱。

18:49.650 --> 18:51.217
Oh.
哦。

18:51.304 --> 18:56.091
I better find out who got
my spell book, and fast.
我最好找出谁得到了
我的咒语书，而且速度很快。

18:56.178 --> 18:57.092
Huh?
啊？

18:57.179 --> 19:00.617
Right after I finish my quiche.
就在我吃完乳蛋饼之后。

19:02.750 --> 19:04.752
- Why is this happening?
- 为什么会发生这种情况？

19:04.839 --> 19:07.015
- Maybe all the weird
stuff I've been cooking
- 也许一切都很奇怪
我一直在煮的东西

19:07.102 --> 19:08.321
caused all of this.
造成了这一切。

19:08.408 --> 19:10.236
[chuckling]
[轻笑]

19:10.323 --> 19:13.064
Would explain the cauldron too.
也会解释一下锅。

19:13.152 --> 19:14.892
And the flying cookbook.
还有飞行食谱。

19:14.979 --> 19:17.852
[suspenseful music]
[悬疑音乐]

19:17.939 --> 19:24.815
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

19:30.473 --> 19:32.562
The cookbook
is using tasty breakfast
食谱
正在使用美味的早餐

19:32.649 --> 19:34.738
treats to create a monster.
治疗来创造一个怪物。

19:34.825 --> 19:36.566
- [roars]
- [咆哮]

19:36.653 --> 19:37.872
[all screaming]
[所有人尖叫]

19:40.614 --> 19:44.661
- Oh, so this is where
my spell book went.
- 哦，这就是地方
我的咒语书不见了。

19:44.748 --> 19:48.230
- [roars]
- [咆哮]

19:49.971 --> 19:51.015
- Ooh, a customer.
- 哦，一位顾客。

19:51.102 --> 19:52.756
Take her order, Squidward.
听她的命令，章鱼哥。

19:52.843 --> 19:55.194
- Uh, thanks, but I
couldn't eat another bite.
- 呃，谢谢，但是我
不能再吃一口了。

19:55.281 --> 19:56.282
[belches]
[打嗝]

19:56.369 --> 19:58.371
I'm here to swap books with you.
我是来和你交换书籍的。

19:58.458 --> 20:01.809
I think my spell book got
mixed up with your cookbook.
我想我的咒语书得到了
和你的食谱混在一起了。

20:01.896 --> 20:05.552
But first, I better take
care of this foodie fiasco.
但首先，我最好采取
照顾这个美食家的惨败。

20:05.639 --> 20:08.555
Flippity floppity food.
软软的食物。

20:08.642 --> 20:11.558
[dramatic music]
[戏剧音乐]

20:11.645 --> 20:17.738
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

20:17.825 --> 20:20.088
[babbling]
[胡说]

20:20.175 --> 20:23.526
Ah!
Not maple syrup.
啊!
不是枫糖浆。

20:23.613 --> 20:25.615
I'm sticky.
我很粘。

20:25.702 --> 20:29.489
So sticky.
太粘了。

20:29.576 --> 20:32.883
Hey, you, the spongy kid
with the wand.
嘿，你这个海绵宝宝
用魔杖。

20:32.970 --> 20:34.189
- That's a spatula.
- 那是一把抹刀。

20:34.276 --> 20:35.625
- My wand.
- 我的魔杖。

20:35.712 --> 20:39.499
- Well, I'll lend you
some of my magic.
- 好吧，我借给你
我的一些魔法。

20:39.586 --> 20:43.242
The only way to stop breakfast
is with its mortal enemy...
停止吃早餐的唯一方法
与它的死敌……

20:43.329 --> 20:44.678
dinner.
晚餐。

20:44.765 --> 20:47.985
- Oh, I can do dinner.
- 哦，我可以做晚饭。

20:48.072 --> 20:51.075
Pippity poppity pot roast.
皮皮蒂罂粟炖肉。

20:51.162 --> 20:52.120
[grunts]
[咕哝]

20:54.383 --> 20:57.256
- [growls]
- [咆哮]

21:04.915 --> 21:08.528
[all yelling]
[大家大喊]

21:08.615 --> 21:10.094
- No.
- 不。

21:10.181 --> 21:12.923
Squidward is not part
of a balanced breakfast,
章鱼哥不是一部分
均衡的早餐，

21:13.010 --> 21:15.361
a triple-decker Krabby Patty.
三层甲板的克拉比帕蒂

21:15.448 --> 21:16.405
- [roars]
- [咆哮]

21:16.492 --> 21:18.364
- With cheese.
- 配奶酪。

21:18.451 --> 21:21.758
Wah!
哇！

21:21.845 --> 21:23.804
- Mmm.
- 嗯。

21:23.891 --> 21:25.849
[grunting]
[咕噜声]

21:25.936 --> 21:28.199
[loud explosion]
[爆炸声]

21:28.287 --> 21:29.723
Ahh!
啊！

21:29.810 --> 21:30.724
Oh!
哦！

21:30.811 --> 21:32.203
[groaning]
[呻吟]

21:32.291 --> 21:34.510
I need a vacation.
我需要一个假期。

21:37.774 --> 21:40.211
- Hey, kid, do you want
to be my apprentice?
- 嘿，孩子，你想要吗？
做我的徒弟？

21:40.299 --> 21:41.822
You got a real knack for magic.
你确实有魔法天赋。

21:41.909 --> 21:43.824
- Thanks.
- 谢谢。

21:43.911 --> 21:45.608
But the only magic
I need is the delicious
但唯一的魔力
我需要的是美味

21:45.695 --> 21:47.480
taste of a Krabby Patty.
蟹肉饼的味道。

21:47.567 --> 21:49.133
- Eh.
- 呃。

21:49.220 --> 21:50.700
A patty?
一块肉饼？

21:50.787 --> 21:52.833
It's a little early for me.
对我来说有点早了。

21:52.920 --> 21:55.575
Unless...
除非...

21:55.662 --> 21:56.576
Hmm.
唔。

21:56.663 --> 22:00.449
A Krabby waffle.
蟹黄华夫饼。

22:00.536 --> 22:03.234
- Ooh, a Krabby waffle, eh?
- 哦，蟹黄华夫饼，嗯？

22:03.322 --> 22:06.803
I have another brilliant idea.
我还有另一个好主意。

22:06.890 --> 22:10.067
We will no longer
be serving breakfast.
我们将不再
正在供应早餐。

22:10.154 --> 22:14.507
From now on, the Krusty Krab
will be serving "brinner."
从现在开始，蟹堡王
将提供“brinner”。

22:14.594 --> 22:17.553
- Ooh, the breakfast-dinner duo.
- 哦，早餐晚餐二人组。

22:17.640 --> 22:21.296
- And this time, I picked
up the new cookbook myself.
- 而这一次，我选择了
我自己写了新的食谱。

22:22.689 --> 22:25.474
- [growls]
- [咆哮]

22:36.006 --> 22:40.141
[ghosts howling]
[鬼魂嚎叫]

22:40.228 --> 22:42.491
Hey, we've got customers.
嘿，我们有顾客了。

嘿，我们有顾客了。